6. What is cat?

The cat command is used to display the contents of a file.

It can also be used to create files, combine files, and append content.

=> Practical Examples

a) Display a file:

cat sample.txt

b) Create a file:

cat > newfile.txt

Type some text and press Ctrl + D to save:

This is my first file.

c) Append content to a file:

cat >> newfile.txt

d) Combine two files:

cat file1.txt file2.txt > combined.txt

e) Display line numbers:

cat -n sample.txt

Note:- What I Learned

I learned how to display, create, append, and combine files using the cat command.

7. touch 

What is touch?

The touch command is used to create an empty file.

It can also update the modification time of an existing file.

=> Practical Examples

Create an empty file:

touch app.conf

Check the file:

ls -l app.conf

Create multiple files:

touch file1.txt file2.txt file3.txt

Update the modification time:

touch app.conf

Note:- What I Learned

I learned how to create empty files and update their modification time using touch.

8. echo

What is echo?

The echo command is used to display text in the terminal.

It is also commonly used in shell scripts and for writing text into files.

=> Practical Examples

Display text:

echo "Hello Linux"

Create a file with text:

echo "This is my configuration" > app.conf

Display the file:

cat app.conf

Append text to a file:

echo "Port=8080" >> app.conf

Display a variable:

NAME="Bilal"
echo "$NAME"

Display the current working directory:

echo "$PWD"

Note:- What I Learned

I learned how to display text, create files, append content, and use variables with the echo command.
